# Side branch commit default (`side/tabpfn-settings`)

When working on the TabPFN / settings-prediction side project:

1. Stay on **`side/tabpfn-settings`**. Do not land TabPFN experiment commits on `main`, `quiz-frontend`, or `quiz-backend`.
2. **Default: commit** meaningful local changes on this branch when a unit of work finishes (code, reports, tables, STATUS). Do not leave finished TabPFN work uncommitted unless the user says to wait.
3. Do **not** commit unrelated dirty files from other worktrees/branches (e.g. quiz quality filters, FE/BE docs). Restore those to HEAD on this branch instead.
4. Do not commit `.worktrees/`, secrets, or large caches. Force-add selected `experiments/tabpfn_settings/artifacts/*` reports/tables when they are part of the deliverable.
5. Push only when the user asks.
